{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you stray and do not perform, etc.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Horayot 8a) that this verse speaks of one who worships idolatry, and it contains a doubling of expression: <b>et all the commandments</b>, etc. — <b>et all that He commanded</b>, etc., which comes to say that he denies the Ten Commandments and all the other commandments that they were commanded through Moses. And apart from their words, it appears that it comes to say that one who worships idolatry is as though he transgresses all negative commandments and nullifies all positive commandments. Corresponding to the nullification of positive commandments, it says ״וְלֹא תַעֲשׂוּ אֵת כָּל הַמִּצְוֹת״ — behold, the nullification of all positive commandments; and corresponding to the transgression of all negative commandments, it says ״אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ אֲלֵיכֶם״. And the verse has conveyed to us a novelty regarding positive commandments and negative commandments: for there are positive commandments that are equivalent to the entire Torah — even so, one who worships idolatry is as though he denies even it. And likewise there are severe negative commandments — behold, he is likewise as one who denies them all, and his punishment is equivalent to all."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:48.021866497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}